kens\": 41, \"tool\": \"save_fact\"}\n./README.md:4:by design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\n./README.md:6:the message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\n./README.md:7:when keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\n./README.md:9:its system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n./README.md:15:prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\n./bot.py:3:Every incoming message is a fresh request: we rebuild the system prompt from\n./bot.py:18:USAGE_LOG = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \"logs\", \"usage.jsonl\")\n./bot.py:48:    facts: list = field(default_factory=list)   # long-term memory, grows via save_fact\n./bot.py:73:# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- system prompt\n./bot.py:92:    equipment, races booked), call save_fact once with a single sentence. Do not save moods or one-off plans.\n./bot.py:133:    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n./bot.py:137:    {\"name\": \"save_fact\", \"description\": \"Remember one durable fact about the athlete.\",\n./bot.py:166:    if name == \"save_fact\":\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
